+/// The launch-shape invariant every full-mask shuffle in the five kernels rests on (dsv41_torch.cu's "WARP ALIGNMENT"
+/// note): the participating lanes are whole warps of consecutive element indices, so no lane is inactive inside a
+/// `__shfl_xor_sync(0xffffffffu, ...)` (undefined behaviour, not a wrong number). It holds because:
+///   * `d % 64 == 0` tiles a warp: `d / 2` (the latent's packed half row) is warp-aligned, so element i's rotary
+///     partner is the neighbour lane's, and the key's 32-element `_fp4_store` scale group is exactly one warp;
+///   * `rd` even keeps the rotary suffix's first pair at an even column (`d - rd`), so the xor-1 exchange stays inside
+///     the (even, odd) pair;
+///   * `block % 32 == 0` makes every stride a whole number of warps (`i += blockDim.x`, `blockDim.x * threadIdx.y`), so
+///     a loop's tail leaves whole warps idle rather than single lanes.
+/// `block` is the `blockDim.x` the launcher passes. The launchers refuse a shape this rejects, so the call sites fall
+/// back to the unfused chain; the query kernel's `hd % 32 == 0` (one head a warp) is checked beside this.
+pub fn warpShapesOk(d: usize, rd: usize, block: usize) bool {
+    return d % 64 == 0 and rd >= 2 and rd % 2 == 0 and (d - rd) % 2 == 0 and block % 32 == 0;
+}
